      "id": "white",
      "name": "Waves",
      "description": "One unbroken field over the hip, thigh, back of the flank and gaskin - a fifth to two-fifths of the horse. Its front edge runs dorso-ventrally and is folded into three to six rounded lobes of even size and even spacing, which is what tells it apart from every other soft-edged field on a horse: this one repeats. It reaches the topline or stops just below it, and runs down as far as the gaskin or the hock. A few detached lobes float a hand's breadth in front of the main edge.",
